# Standard Library Architectural Audit: Boyd OODA Primitives (R1)

File: openOODA/audit/std_arch_boyd_ooda.oot
Status: Certified Complete (R1 First-Principles Verification)

## 1. Boyd's Complete OODA Architecture

Colonel John Boyd modeled decision-making in competitive environments as an adaptive loop.
The system is not a rigid sequence. It includes multiple implicit feedback paths.

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                 BOYD'S COMPLETE OODA ARCHITECTURE                               │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  ┌────────────────┐                                                       ┌─────────────────┐   │
│  │    OBSERVE     │                                                       │       ACT       │   │
│  │  • Sensors     │                                                       │  • Actuators    │   │
│  │  • Noise / DSP │                                                       │  • Capabilities │   │
│  │  • EKF Fusion  │                                                       │  • Conservation │   │
│  └───────┬────────┘                                                       └────────▲────────┘   │
│          │                                                                         │            │
│          │      ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐      │            │
│          │      │                          ORIENT                           │      │            │
│          │      │  • Cultural Heritage     • Genetic Heritage               │      │            │
│          └─────►│  • Previous Experience   • New Information (Observations) │──────┼────────────┤
│                 │  • Analysis & Synthesis (Destruction & Creation)          │      │            │
│                 │  • Epistemic Bounds: Gödel, Heisenberg, Thermodynamics    │      │  Implicit  │
│                 └─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘      │  Guidance  │
│                                               │                                    │  & Control │
│                                               ▼                                    │  (Reflex)  │
│                                     ┌───────────────────┐                          │  (IG&C)    │
│                                     │      DECIDE       │                          │            │
│                                     │  • Game Theory    │                          │            │
│                                     │  • Pareto Opt     │──────────────────────────┘            │
│                                     │  • Optimization   │                                       │
│                                     └───────────────────┘                                       │
│  FEEDBACK LOOPS:                                                                                │
│  • Action -> Observe (Environmental Consequence Sensation)                                      │
│  • Action -> Orient  (Kinetic Confirmation & State Updates)                                     │
│  • Orient -> Observe (Sensory Attention Gating & Focus)                                         │
│  • Orient -> Act     (Implicit Guidance & Control / Autonomic Reflex Bypass)                    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## 2. Observe Primitives & Signal Physics

The Observe primitive ingests external signals, applies filtering, and constructs state vectors.

### 2.1 AESA 4th-Root Radar Range & Scanning Laws
Located in ooda/std/phys/sensors/aesa_radar_laws.oo.
Radar received power P_rx at range R satisfies:
  P_rx = (P_tx * G_tx * G_rx * lambda^2 * sigma) / ((4 * pi)^3 * R^4)
Maximum detection range follows the 4th-root scaling law:
  R = R_0 * ((sigma / sigma_0) * (P / P_0))^(1/4)
For Active Electronically Scanned Arrays, scan loss away from boresight angle theta satisfies:
  G(theta) = G_0 * cos^1.5(theta)  (for |theta| < 90 degrees)
Ground clutter filtering rejects returns where target Doppler closure delta_v matches ground return:
  Notch(delta_v, theta_AOT) = (|theta_AOT - 90 deg| <= 10 deg) AND (|delta_v| <= v_notch)

### 2.2 3-State Flight Altitude EKF Fusion
Located in ooda/std/phys/uav_flight/uav_altitude_kalman_fusion.oo.
State vector x = [z, v_z, a_bias]^T propagates kinematics over interval dt:
  z_(k+1|k) = z_k + v_(z,k) * dt + 0.5 * (a_(z,m) - a_(bias,k)) * dt^2
  v_(z,k+1|k) = v_(z,k) + (a_(z,m) - a_(bias,k)) * dt
  a_(bias,k+1|k) = a_(bias,k)
Covariance propagation includes cross-covariance terms:
  P_(k+1|k) = F * P_(k|k) * F^T + Q
Innovation variance S = P_11 + R.
Kalman gain for velocity incorporates cross-covariance: K_vz = P_21 / S.
Measurement update attenuates all covariance terms: P_(k+1|k+1) = (I - K * H) * P_(k+1|k).

### 2.3 Self-Exciting Hawkes Point Processes
Located in ooda/std/econ/hft_alpha/mm_hawkes_point_process.oo.
Incoming event intensity lambda(t) follows:
  lambda(t) = mu + sum_(t_i < t) alpha * exp(-beta * (t - t_i))
Stationarity requires the spectral radius of excitation matrix Gamma (Gamma_ij = alpha_ij / beta_j)
to be strictly less than unity:
  rho(Gamma) = max_k |lambda_k(Gamma)| < 1.0
For a 2x2 bivariate system, eigenvalues are computed analytically:
  rho(Gamma) = ((alpha_11 + alpha_22) + sqrt((alpha_11 - alpha_22)^2 + 4 * alpha_12 * alpha_21)) / (2 * beta)

## 3. Orient Primitives & Cybernetic Geometry

The Orient primitive synthesizes prior experience, filters noise, and projects mental models.

### 3.1 Ashby's Law of Requisite Variety & Homeostasis
Located in ooda/std/ai/cybernetics/cybernetics.oo.
W. Ross Ashby proved that a regulator achieves stability only when control variety
matches disturbance variety:
  Variety(controller) >= Variety(disturbance)
When error exceeds threshold epsilon, the homeostat triggers an immediate fail-closed quarantine:
  |y(t) - y_setpoint| > epsilon  =>  quarantine_reflex()

### 3.2 Information Geometry: Relative Entropy & Jensen-Shannon Divergence
Located in ooda/std/math/information/relative_entropy.oo.
Kullback-Leibler (KL) divergence measures information gain from prior Q to observation P:
  D_KL(P || Q) = sum_i p_i * ln(p_i / q_i)
Symmetrized Jensen-Shannon Divergence provides a bounded metric distance (0 <= JSD <= ln(2)):
  JSD(P, Q) = 0.5 * D_KL(P || M) + 0.5 * D_KL(Q || M), where M = 0.5 * (P + Q)

## 4. Decide Primitives & Optimization

The Decide primitive selects optimal actions and resolves multi-agent game-theoretic incentives.

### 4.1 2x2 Mixed-Strategy Nash Equilibrium (Player Indifference)
Located in ooda/std/math/game_theory/nash_equilibrium.oo.
Let Player A have payoff matrix A and Player B have payoff matrix B.
Player A chooses row probability p* to make Player B indifferent between columns:
  p* = (b_22 - b_21) / (b_11 - b_12 - b_21 + b_22)
Player B chooses column probability q* to make Player A indifferent between rows:
  q* = (a_22 - a_12) / (a_11 - a_21 - a_12 + a_22)
Conclusion: Strategy p* depends strictly on Matrix B; strategy q* depends strictly on Matrix A.

### 4.2 Quadratic Gradient Descent Lipschitz Stability Bound
Located in ooda/std/math/optimization/optimization_core.oo.
For quadratic objective f(x) = a * x^2 + b * x + c with a > 0:
  Gradient f'(x) = 2*a*x + b, Lipschitz constant L = 2*a.
Gradient descent iteration x_(k+1) = (1 - 2*a*eta)*x_k - eta*b converges if and only if:
  |1 - 2*a*eta| < 1  <=>  0 < eta < 1 / a
Exact stability bound requires division: eta < 1 / a (not multiplication 2 * a).

### 4.3 Exact 2D Lebesgue Measure for Pareto Hypervolume
Located in ooda/std/math/game_theory/pareto_optimality.oo.
Hypervolume indicator is the Lebesgue measure of the union of dominated regions:
  HV(P, r) = Measure( Union_(p in P) [p, r] )
Points sorted by x in ascending order compute disjoint vertical strips without over-counting:
  HV = (x_1 - r_xmin)*(r_y - y_1) + sum_(i=1)^(k-1) (x_(i+1) - x_i)*(r_y - y_(i+1)) + (r_x - x_k)*(r_y - y_k)

## 5. Act Primitives & Capability Security

The Act primitive executes actions under unforgeable tokens and physical conservation laws.

### 5.1 Zero Ambient Authority & The 22 Capability Tokens

| Capability Token | Domain Privilege Granted | Lowered Runtime Hook | Security Invariant |
|---|---|---|---|
| &AllocCap | Linear arena host memory | arena_create, arena_reset | Zero heap leaks |
| &GpuCap | AMD ROCm/HIP kernel & VRAM | hipLaunchKernel, hipMalloc | Device buffer isolation |
| &FsReadCap | Sandboxed filesystem read | read_file, fs_read_dir | OODA_FS_READDIR confined |
| &FsWriteCap | Sandboxed filesystem write | write_file, fs_mkdir | OODA_FS_WRITEDIR confined |
| &NetCap | Raw network packet I/O | sock_raw | Packet boundary check |
| &TcpCap | Outbound TCP client | tcp_connect, tls_connect | Sandboxed endpoint check |
| &UdpCap | Outbound UDP datagrams | udp_send | Datagram size clamp |
| &BindCap | Inbound listening ports | tcp_bind | Authorized port list |
| &ProcessCap | Subprocess lifecycle | sys_spawn, sys_exec | Environment sanitization |
| &ThreadCap | Actor lifecycle & mailbox | thread_spawn, mailbox_send | Concurrency isolation |
| &TimeCap | Monotonic clock & sleeps | now_ms, sleep_ms | Precision clock gating |
| &RandCap | Cryptographic hardware entropy | random, seed | Entropy pool protection |
| &CryptoCap | Hardware crypto accelerators | pqc_encap, pqc_sign | Constant-time execution |
| &EnclaveCap | Secure enclave isolation | enclave_enter, enclave_exit | TEE memory encryption |
| &SysCap | Host OS syscalls (Landlock) | sys_epoll, sys_prctl | Kernel ABI boundary check |

### 5.2 Strict Capability Sealing for GPU Operations
In ooda/oodac/check_cap_util.oo, GPU allocations (gpu_buffer_alloc, gpu_buffer_free, gpu_copy_h2d,
gpu_copy_d2h) require &GpuCap. The permissive fallback oo_cap_require_gpu_or_alloc is dropped.
Host memory remains restricted to &AllocCap.

### 5.3 4-Factor Physical Conservation Laws
Located in ooda/std/phys/conservation_laws.oo. Actuation verifies invariants within epsilon = 10^-6:
1. Total Energy: |E_final - E_initial| <= epsilon
2. Linear Momentum: ||p_final - p_initial|| <= epsilon
3. Angular Momentum: ||L_final - L_initial|| <= epsilon
4. Electric Charge: |Q_final - Q_initial| <= epsilon
